## Decision

BGE-M3 token-level interaction with K-NRM is consistently better than the EmbeddingGemma signed-difference classifier across all three graph-disjoint outer folds. It is the stronger of these two measured pipelines for overall accuracy and macro F1.

The unresolved weakness is Potential Fit discrimination. K-NRM's mean Potential Fit F1 is `0.2114`, below EmbeddingGemma's `0.3080`. The model therefore improves overall three-class performance primarily through much stronger No Fit classification, not through uniformly better separation of all classes.
